.TH WORKFLOW-VERIFIER 1 "August 2026" "workflow-verifier 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
workflow-verifier \- offline semantic verification and concrete CI scenario replay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B workflow-verifier
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
workflow-verifier analyzes GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, and
CircleCI workflows from one deterministic analysis manifest. Network,
source mutation, secrets, and sandbox execution are disabled unless separately
authorized. Unsupported runtime semantics are reported as typed Incomplete
results and are never guessed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Analyze and gate a workflow tree; JSON output is workflow-verifier-report/1.
.TP
.B graph
Emit workflow-verifier-graph/1 JSON or DOT. Graph data is not embedded in a
check report.
.TP
.B resolve
Create or verify a lock-v2 dependency lock. Network access requires
--allow-network and a trusted origin policy.
.TP
.B sandbox plan
Lower an explicit scenario-v1, or --job shorthand, to runner-v2.
.TP
.B sandbox run
Execute only a complete runner-v2 plan in the selected fail-closed backend.
.TP
.B sandbox replay
Verify an evidence-v2 hash chain offline.
.TP
.B doctor
Report backend availability and reasons in text or doctor-v2 JSON.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 pass; 1 finding or policy failure; 2 input or configuration error; 3 strict
incomplete result; 4 internal failure; 5 sandbox infrastructure failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
NO_COLOR disables ANSI color. WORKFLOW_VERIFIER_*_HELPER selects an optional
native helper. Secrets are granted by name at runtime and are not written to
plans or evidence.
.SH FILES
.workflow-verifier.toml is untrusted repository configuration unless explicitly
trusted. Trusted policy must live outside the analyzed repository. Static
analysis reads only files that can affect its result; sandbox execution takes a
separate complete repository snapshot.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/P4suta/workflow-verifier/tree/main/docs
